The setter decorator must be attached to the same property object that the getter created. The typical pattern is:
```python
class C:
    @property
    def x(self):
        return self._x
    @x.setter
    def x(self, value):
        self._x = value
```
If you wrote @property def x(...): ... and later defined a separate function with @property.setter, Python creates a new property instead of modifying the original, leading to the error. Keep the setter directly after the getter and use the same name.

