Write a comment right above a function when its purpose, inputs, or side effects aren't obvious from the name and signature. The comment should briefly state what the function does, describe each parameter (including units or expected format), and note any important side effects or exceptions it may raise. Avoid restating the code line‑by‑line; instead focus on the why and the contract. For example:

