Use inline comments (//) for short notes on a single line of code, especially when the comment explains a tricky expression or a non‑obvious constant. Block comments (/* ... */ or multi‑line //) are better for longer explanations that span several lines, such as describing an algorithm's overall strategy. Keep inline comments brief; if you need more than a sentence, switch to a block comment above the relevant code block. For example:

